        "subject": "LU-17000 obdclass: drop dead sscanf() error checks",
        "message": "LU-17000 obdclass: drop dead sscanf() error checks\n\nstring_to_decimal() tests sscanf() for a negative return.  The kernel's\nvsscanf() only ever returns the number of conversions performed, so\nthose branches are dead; the \"rc < 1\" tests that follow them are what\nactually catches a failed conversion.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: 10547cbf7ad1 (\"LU-18163 obdclass: fix sysfs_memparse()/string_to_size()\")\nSigned-off-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:Opus-5 llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: Id8f952ec9deb61ce13f28e2dbbd78e2de0b4231b\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68498\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: James Simmons <jsimmons@infradead.org>\nReviewed-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\n"
